      "date": "2026-09-30",
      "headline": "The synthetic respondent",
      "text": "Pew Research Center said on September 30th that AI “digital twins” of survey panellists missed real answers by 12.4 points on average across nearly 300 questions, and by more than 15 points on 28% of them. It concluded that AI is not an adequate substitute for polling people.",
